From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 21:53:38 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] selinux: ignore unknown extended permission types instead of
 BUG()

libsepol >= 3.7 emits AVTAB_XPERMS_NLMSG (3) for 'allowxperm ... nlmsg'
rules; Android 15+ policy carries them on the netlink socket classes.
The avtab reader stores the type without looking at it, but
services_compute_xperms_decision() hits BUG() on anything other than
IOCTLFUNCTION/IOCTLDRIVER.

That path is reachable: 'allowxperm domain self:socket_class_set ioctl
unpriv_sock_ioctls' puts IOCTLFUNCTION nodes on the same
(source, target, netlink_route_socket) key as the NLMSG nodes, so the
first ioctl on a route socket walks onto an NLMSG node and oopses.

There is no netlink extended-permission hook in this kernel, so such a
rule can never apply to an ioctl decision.  Skip it (warn once) instead,
which is what any pre-6.13 upstream kernel effectively does.
---
 security/selinux/ss/avtab.h    | 1 +
 security/selinux/ss/services.c | 9 ++++++++-
 2 files changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/security/selinux/ss/avtab.h b/security/selinux/ss/avtab.h
index 1778ce468084..366dd2203fb4 100644
--- a/security/selinux/ss/avtab.h
+++ b/security/selinux/ss/avtab.h
@@ -58,6 +58,7 @@ struct avtab_extended_perms {
 /* These are not flags. All 256 values may be used */
 #define AVTAB_XPERMS_IOCTLFUNCTION	0x01
 #define AVTAB_XPERMS_IOCTLDRIVER	0x02
+#define AVTAB_XPERMS_NLMSG		0x03
 	/* extension of the avtab_key specified */
 	u8 specified; /* ioctl, netfilter, ... */
 	/*
diff --git a/security/selinux/ss/services.c b/security/selinux/ss/services.c
index 121b5cfe2d20..ad55c2ee05ef 100644
--- a/security/selinux/ss/services.c
+++ b/security/selinux/ss/services.c
@@ -967,7 +967,14 @@ void services_compute_xperms_decision(struct extended_perms_decision *xpermd,
 					xpermd->driver))
 			return;
 	} else {
-		BUG();
+		/*
+		 * AVTAB_XPERMS_NLMSG or something newer.  This kernel has no
+		 * netlink extended permission hook, so the rule cannot apply
+		 * to an ioctl decision; skip it instead of oopsing.
+		 */
+		pr_warn_once("SELinux: unknown extended permission type %u ignored\n",
+			     node->datum.u.xperms->specified);
+		return;
 	}
 
 	if (node->key.specified == AVTAB_XPERMS_ALLOWED) {
